 "id": "169-9",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "One of our key practices is that we never use profilers.",
  "It's important that you avoid using them in your code as well.",
  "This helps us maintain consistency and makes our code easier to read and understand.",
  "They might vary from project to project, so it's good to stay updated.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns.",
  "Each meeting will span two days.",
  "I'll handle the initial presentations and overview, and then we can tag-team the Q&A sessions.",
  "Now, regarding the travel arrangements for the conferences later in the year, I'll be in touch with more details as we get closer to the dates.",
  "From now on, when naming attributes, always start them with 't_'.",
  "This is to maintain consistency and make our code more readable.",
  "Also, remember to include assert statements in your functions to verify that the inputs meet the expected criteria.",
  "No, that's all for now, Bob.",
  "Just remember to include them and you'll be on the right track.",
  "From now on, I want you to incorporate a profiler into your development process.",
  "Ideally, you'd want to profile your code regularly, especially when working on performance-critical sections.",
  "It's a good practice to profile your code after making significant changes or adding new features.",
  "That way, you can catch any potential issues early on."
 ],
